Sectoral shock propagation. The primary statistic is the total output loss caused by a 50 per cent capacity cut lasting eight quarters; the amplification ratios are reported alongside with the caveat that they divide by the shocked sector's output share and therefore overweight small sectors. Generated by scripts/paper_tables.py from results/B3. Source: reference_results/ (the Lead's independent reference run; cross-checked against the experiment layer in reference_results/CROSSCHECK.md).
